          "cached_tokens": 995,
          "reasoning_tokens": 0,
          "finish_reason": "length",
          "answer_excerpt": "# Technical Analysis of Plant Condition-Monitoring Records (Records 0000000\u20130000017)\n\n## 1. Scope and Method\n\nThis report analyzes 18 condition-monitoring records spanning six asset classes (condensers, scrubbers, pumps, heat exchangers, pipelines, valves, reactors, separators) across 18 stations. Each record contains five measured parameters: pressure (kPa), temperature (\u00b0C), flow (m\u00b3/h), vibration (mm/s RMS), and efficiency (%).\n\nBecause the dataset contains no nameplate data, design baselines, or historical trends, the analysis relies on:\n\n1. **Cross-population statistics** \u2014 comparing each unit against the fleet distribution to flag statistical outliers.\n2. **Asset-class expectations** \u2014 typical operating envelopes for each equipment type.\n3. **Internal consistency checks** \u2014 whether the five parameters for a given unit are physically plausible *together* (e.g., a hot condenser with low flow and high vibration tells a different story than a hot condenser with high flow).\n\nFleet statistics for context:\n\n| Parameter | Min | Max | Mean | Approx. spread |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| Pressure (kPa) | 132 | 882 |",
